            "keyPoints": [
                "India grew 7.8% in April-June 2026, beating the 7.1% consensus and the RBI's own 7.0% estimate for the quarter.",
                "The war that started on 28 February 2026 shut the Strait of Hormuz; Gulf crude exports fell to about 9 million barrels a day from roughly 17 million before the conflict.",
                "India imports 88.7% of its crude, so the shock landed on the import bill, not on output: $63.4bn in April-July, up 57% year-on-year.",
                "Growth came from investment (+11.9%) and manufacturing (+9.2%), not from a consumption boom.",
                "Russia stayed India's largest crude supplier through August 2026, cushioning the Middle East disruption.",
                "Inflation rose to 4.45% in July, a 19-month high, but stayed inside the RBI's 2-6% band; the repo rate was held at 5.25% on 5 August.",
                "The RBI still sees only 6.7% for the full year FY27, so the strong first quarter is expected to moderate.",
                "Some economists have questioned how much of the headline number reflects the revised GDP methodology and base year rather than underlying momentum."
            ],
